---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';import GuideCard from '../../components/GuideCard.astro';import {categories} from '../../config';import {publishedArticles} from '../../lib/content';
export function getStaticPaths(){return categories.map(category=>({params:{category:category.slug},props:{category}}));}
const {category}=Astro.props;const posts=(await publishedArticles()).filter(post=>post.data.category===category.slug);
---
<Base title={`${category.name} for Excel & Google Sheets`} description={`${category.description} Practical ${category.name.toLowerCase()} examples, clear procedures, and explicit verification limits.`} breadcrumbs={[{name:category.name,url:`/${category.slug}/`}]}><header class="page-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Explore / {category.name}</p><h1>{category.name}</h1><p>{category.description}</p></header>{posts.length>0?<div class="guide-grid section">{posts.map(post=><GuideCard post={post}/>)}</div>:<section class="prose info-content"><h2>A small example you can take apart</h2><p>Our templates begin with transparent practice data, rather than opaque workbooks or macros. Download the sample below, keep an unchanged copy, and choose a task before opening it in a spreadsheet app.</p><p><a href="/examples/sales-practice.csv" download>Download the fictional sales CSV</a>. It contains four records with region, status, and numeric revenue. There is no personal or customer data.</p><h3>A check before you build</h3><p>The two North / Closed records contain 240 and 360, so their total is 600. The South / Closed record and the North / Open record must not contribute. Compare your own formula with that expectation before adapting it to real data.</p><p>This example is manually calculated and checked in an automated arithmetic assertion. It is not an Excel or Google Sheets execution report. CSV import may reinterpret fields; use an import dialog and choose column types deliberately.</p><h3>Build the next step yourself</h3><p>Use the <a href="/formulas/sumifs-with-dates/">SUMIFS date guide</a> for criteria design, <a href="/data-cleaning/import-csv-preserve-zeros-dates/">the CSV import guide</a> to preserve identifiers, or the <a href="/tools/formula-finder/">Formula Finder</a> for a small syntax example. Keep your source data separate from calculations and inspect edge cases before copying a formula across a larger sheet.</p><p>Additional full-workbook templates will be listed here when they have a defined purpose and verifiable results. We do not label unfinished downloads as tested templates.</p></section>}</Base>
